WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:03.879
If you want to hear my ideas about the meaning
of Midsommar, stick around to the end of this

00:00:03.880 --> 00:00:04.840
video.

00:00:08.020 --> 00:00:10.500
Welcome back to Things You Missed.

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:13.769
I'm not going to attempt to fully explain
every little image in this movie, because

00:00:13.769 --> 00:00:17.140
there's so much packed into it, and I'm not
familiar with the culture that it's based

00:00:17.140 --> 00:00:18.140
on.

00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:20.410
So in this video I'm just going to tell you
what I did notice, what connections I made

00:00:20.410 --> 00:00:22.020
and my interpretations are.

00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:25.650
So the movie starts with this painting of
the village divided up into four sections,

00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:27.340
Spring, Summer, Fall and Winter.

00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:30.740
This image establishes the cyclical themes
that we'll see in the movie: the cycle of

00:00:30.740 --> 00:00:35.300
seasons throughout one year, the cycle of
life, death, impregnation and rebirth and

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:37.680
the actual class system that the commune uses.

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:41.100
The Swedish-American friend Pelle explains
that children under 18 are considered to be

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:45.280
in Spring section of their lives Spring is
known for leaves starting to grow on the trees,

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:49.130
so it goes along with the idea of their children
growing up, maybe even hitting puberty and

00:00:49.130 --> 00:00:50.130
growing hair.

00:00:50.130 --> 00:00:53.710
Ages 18 to 36 are considered Summer, when
the trees are at their fullest.

00:00:53.710 --> 00:00:57.050
Our characters fall in this age range, and
they in their prime during this movie.

00:00:57.050 --> 00:01:01.010
The events take place on Dani's birthday drawing
attention to the fact that we are supposed

00:01:01.010 --> 00:01:02.710
to notice that they're in their prime.

00:01:02.710 --> 00:01:05.920
There's even talk at the beginning that the
boyfriend Christian could be wasting his time

00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:08.799
with Dani, they tell him he could be with
that waitress right now.

00:01:08.799 --> 00:01:10.760
And of course, the movie takes place in summer.

00:01:10.760 --> 00:01:14.210
I'm sure you didn't miss the title of the
movie: Midsommar.

00:01:14.210 --> 00:01:18.450
Ages 36-54 are Autumn, and this is when the
leaves start to fall off the trees and they

00:01:18.450 --> 00:01:19.680
start to decline.

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:23.710
This could be seen as when adults start losing
hair and reaching the end of their reproductive

00:01:23.710 --> 00:01:24.710
fertility.

00:01:24.710 --> 00:01:29.520
Ages 54-72 are Winter, which maybe explains
why the cultists were so upset when Christian's

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:32.979
friend Mark pees on the dead tree, because
they see it as a symbol for their own passed

00:01:32.979 --> 00:01:33.979
elders.

00:01:33.979 --> 00:01:37.180
When Dani asks what happens after 72, he gives
her a cut-throat gesture.

00:01:37.180 --> 00:01:40.500
I think we see this happen in the ceremony
on the second day they are there, where two

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:44.220
of the oldest looking villagers, referred
to as "the ones", lead the feast, and then

00:01:44.220 --> 00:01:46.763
sacrifice some blood on the runes at the top
of the cliff.

00:01:46.763 --> 00:01:50.150
The American characters are shocked by the
diving scene that follows.

00:01:50.150 --> 00:01:52.560
Another cycle we see in the movie is the day
night cycle.

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:55.119
Dani has a painting in her living room of
two moons in the night sky.

00:01:55.119 --> 00:01:59.049
It provides a contrast to their destination
in Sweden, where the days last twice as long

00:01:59.049 --> 00:02:00.049
as the nights.

00:02:00.049 --> 00:02:03.479
When they enter the village they come through
this big sun shaped structure, and the platform

00:02:03.479 --> 00:02:05.610
in the center of the village has a sun painted
on it.

00:02:05.610 --> 00:02:09.119
The city they come from seems to be in the
middle of Winter, so they go from Winter with

00:02:09.119 --> 00:02:11.459
two moons, to summer with two suns.

00:02:11.459 --> 00:02:14.840
Also, when Christian is eventually garbed
in the cult's traditional clothing towards

00:02:14.840 --> 00:02:17.630
the end of the movie, a sun and moon can be
seen on his robes.

00:02:17.630 --> 00:02:21.130
There are more symbols about the circle of
life, like when they first arrive and there

00:02:21.130 --> 00:02:24.430
is an older woman chanting prayers in what
I'm assuming is Swedish.

00:02:24.430 --> 00:02:28.000
There are not always subtitles showing during
these prayers, but this time there are, she

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:30.060
says "spirits back to the dead".

00:02:30.060 --> 00:02:33.770
Whenever Dani drinks that tea that gives her
the drug trip, she sees grass growing on her

00:02:33.770 --> 00:02:37.680
feet, an image commonly associated with the
idea that the dead are taken back by nature.

00:02:37.680 --> 00:02:41.310
When the tourists get freaked out by the cliff
jumping scene, one of the village elders tries

00:02:41.310 --> 00:02:45.270
to calm the girl down by explaining that life
is a circle, and it's actually a great joy

00:02:45.270 --> 00:02:48.819
for them to die and give their spirits to
the upcoming newborns -- and I know I'm not

00:02:48.819 --> 00:02:52.380
supposed to put my opinion but that guy who
drove his leg didn't look too joyful.

00:02:52.380 --> 00:02:57.470
I could be wrong but in my culture, screaming
in fucking agony is not typically a sign of

00:02:57.470 --> 00:02:58.470
joy.

00:02:58.470 --> 00:03:01.670
When Dani and Christian talk about it afterwards,
he says that it was shocking, but his tone

00:03:01.670 --> 00:03:02.670
of voice says otherwise.

00:03:02.670 --> 00:03:06.129
He suggests that they keep an open mind and
try to acclimate to the culture.

00:03:06.129 --> 00:03:10.440
From this point on in the movie they transition
from spectators of the ritual to participants,

00:03:10.440 --> 00:03:13.670
becoming a part of the ritual, taking on the
traditional clothing, and eventually Dani

00:03:13.670 --> 00:03:16.980
is even able to speak their language during
the dancing competition.

00:03:16.980 --> 00:03:20.920
As they become apart of the cult, they become
a part of the cycle, and one of the women,

00:03:20.920 --> 00:03:22.900
Maya takes an interest in Christian.

00:03:22.900 --> 00:03:24.690
Dani later becomes the May Queen.

00:03:24.690 --> 00:03:29.690
Maya, May, they could both be a reference
to the calendar month of May, where Spring

00:03:29.690 --> 00:03:31.060
starts to become Summer.

00:03:31.060 --> 00:03:35.129
Pelle explains that Maya was recently approved
for some ritual, it basically means she's

00:03:35.129 --> 00:03:40.080
allowed to reproduce, because she too is going
from Spring to Summer and becoming an adult.

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:41.849
Pregnancy is focused on throughout the movie.

00:03:41.849 --> 00:03:45.050
In the very beginning, the Christian and his
friends are out at the restaurant, one of

00:03:45.050 --> 00:03:48.150
the friends sees their waitress walk away
and says, "you could be getting that girl

00:03:48.150 --> 00:03:49.159
pregnant right now."

00:03:49.159 --> 00:03:52.690
Kind of a weird thing to say if not for the
circle of life metaphor.

00:03:52.690 --> 00:03:54.430
Also, the way they are seated at the table.

00:03:54.430 --> 00:03:58.379
They are seated in an arc similar to the way
the women are standing around Christian and

00:03:58.379 --> 00:04:00.520
Maya during the impregnation ritual.

00:04:00.520 --> 00:04:03.510
There's also a picture frames above the table
of a woman bending over.

00:04:03.510 --> 00:04:08.010
The shot is composed so that only her breasts
are in frame, another parallel to the ritual.

00:04:08.010 --> 00:04:11.870
That's the most literal reference to the rebirth
metaphor, there are also more symbolic ones,

00:04:11.870 --> 00:04:15.480
such as all the women in the commune dancing
in a circle around this phallic structure.

00:04:15.480 --> 00:04:19.299
During the feast after the big dancing competition,
an overhead shot shows a food sculpture in

00:04:19.299 --> 00:04:23.610
the middle of the table representing an unclothed
woman and I'm the next shot, the phallic structure

00:04:23.610 --> 00:04:25.479
is lined up over the body of this woman.

00:04:25.479 --> 00:04:28.840
There are some images from the beginning of
the movie before they go to Sweden that come

00:04:28.840 --> 00:04:30.249
back later in the movie.

00:04:30.249 --> 00:04:33.509
Above Dani's bed at her apartment there's
a picture of a bear kissing a girl.

00:04:33.509 --> 00:04:37.759
Dani's boyfriend ends up inside of a hollowed
out bear for the final ritual of the movie.

00:04:37.759 --> 00:04:41.669
In that room Christian is taken to so the
older lady can ask him to impregnate Maya,

00:04:41.669 --> 00:04:45.610
there is an image of a bear on fire on the
wall, another foreshadowing of his fate.

00:04:45.610 --> 00:04:48.289
In Christian's friend's apartment, there is
a similar foreshadowing.

00:04:48.289 --> 00:04:51.680
He has a framed picture of the scarecrow from
The Wizard of Oz.

00:04:51.680 --> 00:04:55.300
In that final burning ritual, there are people
whose corpses are stuffed with hay like a

00:04:55.300 --> 00:04:56.300
human scarecrow.

00:04:56.300 --> 00:04:59.990
Also, during that scene in the apartment,
after Dani shows up everyone kind of bails

00:04:59.990 --> 00:05:01.610
out besides her and Pelle.

00:05:01.610 --> 00:05:05.919
He seems genuinely interested in her I think
he already knows she's fit to be the May Queen

00:05:05.919 --> 00:05:07.430
and join his family.

00:05:07.430 --> 00:05:09.720
He tells her “I am so happy you are coming”.

00:05:09.720 --> 00:05:14.059
Then when the whole group arrives, the village
elder says, "We are so happy to have you,"

00:05:14.059 --> 00:05:16.740
only making eye contact with Dani as he says
so.

00:05:16.740 --> 00:05:20.449
Then when Pelle and Dani have the one on one
talk, he again emphasizes his pleasure that

00:05:20.449 --> 00:05:21.449
she came with.

00:05:21.449 --> 00:05:25.199
He challenges the idea that she is really
happy dating Christian and tells her the story

00:05:25.199 --> 00:05:28.309
of how his parents died and the family was
there for him.

00:05:28.309 --> 00:05:32.449
Dani and Christian become more and more distant
during this time, which is visually conveyed

00:05:32.449 --> 00:05:35.729
when he gives her the birthday cake with the
candle and literally can't keep the flame

00:05:35.729 --> 00:05:36.879
between them burning.

00:05:36.879 --> 00:05:40.449
Pelle explains that the family didn't bicker
over what's theirs and what's not.

00:05:40.449 --> 00:05:43.970
We see this because the babies are raised
by the community, not just the parents.

00:05:43.970 --> 00:05:47.059
When Dani looks through the keyhole and sees
her boyfriend cheating on her, a group of

00:05:47.059 --> 00:05:52.849
several women cry and suffer with her in contrast
to her crying on her boyfriend's lap with

00:05:52.849 --> 00:05:54.520
him not really reacting.

00:05:54.520 --> 00:05:57.520
Christian and his friend Josh bicker over
who gets to write the thesis paper on this

00:05:57.520 --> 00:06:00.259
community, but they recommend that the two
share the topic.

00:06:00.259 --> 00:06:04.069
I think this conversation Pelle has with Dani
helps me understand the character arc that

00:06:04.069 --> 00:06:06.679
Dani goes through in the movie and how the
cult helps her get there.

00:06:06.679 --> 00:06:10.189
At the beginning she’s too emotionally dependant
on her boyfriend, and she’s afraid that

00:06:10.189 --> 00:06:13.099
she leans on him too much, which is only worsened
by her family tragedy.

00:06:13.099 --> 00:06:16.309
He is considering breaking up with her because
it’s too much for him.

00:06:16.309 --> 00:06:20.089
Then, she is introduced to the family, and
she sees how they have this community to support

00:06:20.089 --> 00:06:21.089
each other.

00:06:21.089 --> 00:06:23.620
Pelle gives her thoughtful gifts, and she
becomes a part of the family after winning

00:06:23.620 --> 00:06:26.149
the dance competition and becoming the May
Queen.

00:06:26.149 --> 00:06:29.710
At the end of the movie, they ask her to pick
the next sacrifice and she essentially becomes

00:06:29.710 --> 00:06:33.839
the one to break up with Christian and become
a permanent part of the family when she chooses

00:06:33.840 --> 00:06:34.360
him.

00:06:38.240 --> 00:06:42.360
Now as far as the actual rune characters seen
all over the village go, again, I don’t

00:06:42.369 --> 00:06:45.800
know the culture and I don’t really have
a way of translating them, but here’s what

00:06:45.800 --> 00:06:47.370
I was able to figure out throughout the film.

00:06:47.370 --> 00:06:50.379
There are two characters that come up over
and over again.

00:06:50.379 --> 00:06:53.639
First there’s this R shaped one, which is
sometimes seen rotated or flipped.

00:06:53.639 --> 00:06:56.969
It’s on the birthday drawing that Dani receives,
at the top of the cliff where the jumping

00:06:56.969 --> 00:07:01.050
ritual takes place, on Dani’s robes and
on the clothes Christian receives.

00:07:01.050 --> 00:07:04.650
It can also be seen on the doors to the room
where the impregnation ritual takes place,

00:07:04.650 --> 00:07:07.229
and I’m pretty sure it shows up in more
spots around the commune.

00:07:07.229 --> 00:07:10.509
This is the only symbol in the village that
I know the meaning of, because one of the

00:07:10.509 --> 00:07:14.179
of cult members points to it in the book of
rune characters and says it represents grief.

00:07:14.180 --> 00:07:16.720
It’s obvious why it’s so often associated
with Dani.

00:07:21.060 --> 00:07:23.529
The other one that appears a lot is this hourglass
shape.

00:07:23.529 --> 00:07:27.309
It shows up in the weird comic strip looking
thing that they refer to as a love story for

00:07:27.309 --> 00:07:30.530
some reason and on both characters’ outfits
and around the village.

00:07:30.530 --> 00:07:33.919
Most of the meals that they eat are done so
a table that forms this shape when viewed

00:07:33.919 --> 00:07:38.099
from overhead and the pattern that the fire
burns in the final ritual also resembles this

00:07:38.099 --> 00:07:39.099
shape.

00:07:39.099 --> 00:07:41.580
Let me know if the comments if you have ideas
on what it could mean.

00:07:41.580 --> 00:07:45.360
Although this is only the second film by the
director, Ari Aster, there are a number of

00:07:45.360 --> 00:07:47.199
director's trademarks that are already evident.

00:07:47.199 --> 00:07:51.330
This part of the video will contain spoilers
for his first movie, Hereditary.

00:07:51.330 --> 00:07:55.279
Family tragedy occurs in both movies, Midsommar
opens with the death of Dani's sister and

00:07:55.279 --> 00:07:58.959
parents, and Hereditary shows the decapitation
of the daughter, Charlie.

00:07:58.959 --> 00:08:00.569
Reincarnation is a theme in both movies.

00:08:00.569 --> 00:08:04.599
In Midsommar it's implied that the spirits
of "the ones" are reincarnated into the Maya's

00:08:04.599 --> 00:08:05.599
baby.

00:08:05.599 --> 00:08:09.099
Hereditary is all about reincarnating this
demon named King Paimon.

00:08:09.099 --> 00:08:11.309
Obviously both movies center around cults.

00:08:11.309 --> 00:08:15.209
This next one almost seems to be not only
an Ari Aster trope, but also an A24 trope

00:08:15.209 --> 00:08:17.759
and seems to be turning into a horror genre
trope lately as well.

00:08:17.759 --> 00:08:22.150
I'm talking, of course, about using naked
people, and more specifically naked old people

00:08:22.150 --> 00:08:23.150
for scares.

00:08:23.150 --> 00:08:25.590
Not sure how this one got started, I think
it may have been It Follows.

00:08:25.590 --> 00:08:28.939
So that’s what I noticed about Midsommar,
and I’m sure there’s more that I missed,

00:08:28.939 --> 00:08:31.259
so if you caught anything, let me know in
the comments.

00:08:31.259 --> 00:08:35.050
If you want to see the Things You Missed episode
I did on Hereditary then click the video on

00:08:35.050 --> 00:08:39.729
the left and remember to subscribe to CZsWorld
for new horrors every week, ring the deathbell

00:08:39.729 --> 00:08:43.129
for notifications and I’ll see you in the
next one.

00:08:43.129 --> 00:08:45.290
Assuming we both survive.

